;; sources.sexp — pinned specification sources, converted from sources.toml by
;; scripts/convert_dossier.py (SOT-FORMAT.4). One document form; validate with
;;   python3 scripts/check_sexp_schema.py sources.sexp schema/sources.sexp
;; Round-trip: `python3 scripts/convert_dossier.py verify sources.toml sources.sexp` — data-equal, comment census exact.

(comment "profiles/rv64i-lab-v0/sources.toml — the pinned specification sources for this profile." "" "⛔ WHAT A HASH HERE DOES AND DOES NOT PIN. `sha256` is the digest of the rendered HTML page" "as served at `retrieved`. The **normative identity** is `revision` plus the chapter's own" "stated version. A site template change alters the digest without altering the specification," "and a specification erratum could in principle alter the text without altering the URL. So a" "digest mismatch is a signal to RE-READ and re-confirm the locators, not proof of a semantic" "change — and a digest match is not proof that the normative text is unchanged either, only" "that the artifact we read is the artifact you are reading." "" "Re-derive with `scripts/fetch_sources.sh` (on demand; it needs the network, so it is" "deliberately NOT a commit gate)." "" "Terms: not yet resolved. These artifacts are READ, not redistributed — they are fetched into" "the untracked `target/sources/` working area and no copy is committed. Rule SRC-01 requires" "the actual applicable terms to be recorded before relying on or shipping an artifact;" "\"shipping\" is the part not yet reached. Open question OQ-4 in DOSSIER.md owns it." "⛔ NAME THE PUBLICATION, NOT JUST THE VERSION. `v20260120` identifies nothing on its own, and" "that ambiguity has already cost someone real work: an external investigation searched" "github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual for a `v20260120` release, found the tags jump 2026-01-17 →" "2026-01-21, found that the release PDFs number RV32I §2 and RV64I §4, and concluded that this" "profile's §1.1 / §3.1 citations matched no public build. The deduction was right and the" "conclusion was wrong: these are TWO DIFFERENT PUBLICATIONS of the same specification." "" "github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual  — the source repository and its release PDFs. Numbers" "\"Introduction\" as Chapter 1, so RV32I is §2, RV64I §4." "docs.riscv.org  (pinned here)      — the RISC-V Ratified Specifications Library. Renders" "\"Introduction\" as unnumbered front matter, so RV32I is" "§1.1 and RV64I is §3.1 — which is what every locator in" "definitions/riscv/rv64i.sem.sexp uses." "" "Verified 2026-09-14: all three pinned URLs return HTTP 200 and bytes identical to the digests" "below, and `scripts/check_citations.py` resolves 52 of 52 citations against them. A version" "string without its publication is not an identity.")
(sources (publication "RISC-V Ratified Specifications Library (docs.riscv.org)") (not_this_publication "github.com/riscv/riscv-isa-manual releases — different section numbering") (revision "v20260120") (base_url "https://docs.riscv.org/reference/isa/v20260120/unpriv") (retrieved "2026-09-13") (work_dir "target/sources/riscv-v20260120") (comment "repo-volume, untracked") (source (id "RVI-INTRO") (file "intro.html") (title "Introduction :: RISC-V Ratified Specifications Library") (sha256 "3d65f713115bfd58f783fcebcce3f243f508d0af71bbac79a59e5ff79e13bf0c") (bytes 69772) (http_status 200) (supplies "execution-environment interface (EEI) and hart definitions; the four trap effects; the meaning of UNSPECIFIED")) (source (id "RVI-RV32I") (file "rv32.html") (title "1.1. RV32I Base Integer Instruction Set, Version 2.1") (chapter_version "2.1") (sha256 "3b20e92f067509535f95883832e84b32dbea43a29e1347b7925c374213ad75ec") (bytes 107630) (http_status 200) (supplies "the base integer ISA that RV64I modifies: register state, formats, control transfer, load/store, FENCE, ECALL/EBREAK, HINTs")) (source (id "RVI-RV64I") (file "rv64.html") (title "3.1. RV64I Base Integer Instruction Set, Version 2.1") (chapter_version "2.1") (sha256 "6eadb316c2d535ccb87a7a6feb03ff54af6f4b5bbeb5c1a5102a02af81f13abd") (bytes 49246) (http_status 200) (supplies "the RV64I deltas: XLEN=64, the *W instruction family, 6-bit shift amounts, LWU/LD/SD, RV64I HINT table")))
